      "writtenOn": "2019-09-23T18:42:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We will never try to access a buffer on the CPU that didn\u0027t have the CPU flags set. \n\nWe added this because we thought that there could be times when a buffer was allocated with the CPU flags set but the format definition was too vague for generic android code to operate on the buffer.\n\nHowever, as I am going through the formats it looks like that may not be the case. Is there ever a time when CPU flags are set but the buffer could be in an unexpected/un-generically-defined way?",
      "parentUuid": "a4bc659c_dda89df7",
